(4a) Exact identities of the Collatz repunits
    for every n <= 2*10^5: the initial run of odd T-steps has length exactly v_2(n+1), and along it T^j(n) + 1 = (3/2)^j (n+1)  [the odd branch is the dilation by 3/2 about the fixed point -1].
    k <= 400: T^j(2^k-1) = 3^j 2^(k-j) - 1 for j <= k, T^(k+1)(2^k-1) = (3^k-1)/2 (the base-3 repunit); v_2(3^k-1) = 1 (k odd), v_2(k)+2 (k even) [lifting the exponent]; sigma((3^k-1)/2) = 1 (k even), 2 (k odd).
    2 <= k <= 300: trunk (4^k-1)/3: T = 2^(2k-1), total stopping time 2k, height 2^(2k-1), stopping time 2.
    odd k <= 301: W = (2^k+1)/3: T(W) = 2^(k-1)+1, T^(1+2i)(W) = 3^i 2^(k-1-2i) + 1 (so T^k(W) = 3^((k-1)/2)+1), stopping time 5 (k >= 5; 4 at k = 3); on the 3n-1 sheet T_-(W) = 2^(k-1): the minus trunk.
    even length: R_(2j)^(-2) = -(4^j-1)/3 and T_-(R) = -2^(2j-1): the negative trunk of the 3n-1 sheet (the nu-image of the 3n+1 trunk).
    k <= 300: base-10 repunits T^(2+2i)(R_k) = 3^i 5^k 2^(k-2-2i) + 1 (2+2i <= k): the (10)-pattern that shadows the cycle {1,2}.
